	<ouc:properties label="metadata">
		<title>Meet ISSI’s Academic Coordinator | Lake Tahoe Community College</title>
		<meta name="Description" content="Meet the Academic Coordinator of LTCC’s Intensive Spanish Summer Institute (ISSI) and learn about the leadership and expertise guiding this immersive Spanish language program." />
	</ouc:properties>
	
	<ouc:div label="gallery" group="Everyone" button-text="Select Slider">
		<ouc:editor wysiwyg="gallery" csspath="/_resources/ou/editor/wysiwyg.css" cssmenu="/_resources/ou/editor/styles.txt"/>		
	</ouc:div>
	
	<ouc:div label="main-content" group="Everyone" button-text="Main Content"><ouc:editor csspath="/_resources/ou/editor/wysiwyg.css" cssmenu="/_resources/ou/editor/styles.txt" wysiwyg-class="main-content"/><h4><img style="float: left; padding-right: 1.2rem;" title="Sarah Harmon - ISSI Academic Coodinator Photo" src="https://www.ltcc.edu/_resources/images/25_sharmon_headshot.jpg" alt="Sarah Harmon - ISSI Academic Coodinator" width="250" height="334" />Sarah Harmon</h4>
<div class="elementToProof">
<div data-ogsc="">
<div>
<p>Since 2022, Sarah has been an integral part of the ISSI team, initially joining as an instructor and later taking on the role of Academic Coordinator for the 2022-23 academic year. With a deep passion for teaching, Sarah finds joy in guiding students on their journey of self-expression through various linguistic skills. She thrives on showcasing different aspects of language, culture, and humanity, believing in the transformative power of education.</p>
<p><span style="font-size: inherit; background-color: #fffdfd; color: var(--cms-region--primary-black);">As a seasoned educator,</span><span style="font-size: inherit; background-color: #fffdfd; color: var(--cms-region--primary-black);"> Sarah is dedicated to supporting new ISSI students. When asked for tips and tricks, she encourages students to attend as many ISSI breakout sessions as possible. They offer valuable opportunities for interaction and growth. Additionally, she encourages students to fully embrace their newfound Spanish skills during the program and to seize every chance to practice and apply what they've learned. And most importantly, Sarah emphasizes the importance of enjoying the experience, reminding students to have fun and appreciate the unique atmosphere and community that ISSI offers.</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p>With Sarah Harmon as the Academic Coordinator, ISSI students can expect a nurturing and enriching environment for student success. Her dedication to fostering a love for language and culture makes her an invaluable asset to the ISSI community.&nbsp;</p>
<h4><img style="float: left; padding-right: 1.2rem;" title="Brandon Scutt" src="{{f:80357442}}" alt="A European-American man with a bald head, glasses and a beard" width="250" height="350" />&nbsp;Brandon Scutt</h4>
<p>Since 2018, Brandon has been a dedicated member of the ISSI family, beginning his journey as an instructor and now stepping into the role of Co-Coordinator. With a Master&rsquo;s degree in Spanish Literature and 15 years of experience in both high school and college classrooms, Brandon finds his greatest joy in helping students unlock new worlds through language. He is a passionate advocate for storytelling and full immersion, believing that education is most transformative when it feels like a true adventure. By integrating his love for music and film into his teaching, he strives to showcase the vibrant, human side of the Spanish-speaking world. As a seasoned educator, Brandon is committed to guiding students through the unique intensity of the ISSI program. When asked for his best advice, he encourages students to treat every moment as a chance for discovery, whether in a formal session or a casual conversation. He believes that the "magic" of ISSI happens when students lean into the discomfort of a new language and embrace the process of authentic communication. Above all, Brandon reminds students to let the music and culture of the program fuel their progress, ensuring they leave not just with better Spanish, but with a lasting connection to a global community</p>
</div>
</div>
</div></ouc:div>

